It has been a very hot week, but it turns out I like the heat and don't
mind being all sweaty. Let's go!

Tuesday
Today we had a great DCM (District Council Meeting), even if it was Just
over video chat. Afterwards we did some fire housing, and were able to meet
some really nice people that weren't interested in our church, but It was
still a good experience. We also went and ate Dominos Pizza, which I
haaaaate in America (unpopular opinion). It was Edible but the Pizza Hut I
had here was way better. To end off the day we had some more sword practice
with Shiko, as well as a little bit of guitar stuff too. It was pretty
funny, this time he brought like 4 foam Kids swords, a fake rubber knife,
and some foam nunchucks (no idea how to spell that). It was pretty awesome
lol.

Wednesday
This morning We peeled onions for 3 hours with a guy we helped weed with a
while ago. We had a good chance to talk with him, and he is interested in
playing spikeball sometime together. We were able to talk a bit about our
purpose as missionaries, but we are hoping we can ask him about more Gospel
stuff when we meet again. We had a 30 minute lesson with Hiroko about the
Restoration later, before we headed off to the monthly Kodomo Shokudo,
where theres a bunch of free food. This time we attempted to help out, but
we mostly just stood around lol. Later we had Eikaiwa and ping pong at the
church, which was great as usual!

Thursday
Today we did some weeding for Kanata=E5=85=84=E5=BC=9F, and talked about Am=
erican movies
among other random things. It was super rainy so we were mostly inside
today doing weekly planning and media work. It was definitely kind of a
slump.

Friday
Today we had an Eikaiwa Video call with Aime, and we also had a lesson at
the church with Sakurako=E3=81=95=E3=82=93! We invited her to pray about wh=
at we taught,
and she said she will. We also showed her the Baptismal Font and talked
about Baptism too. She's super prepared for Baptism, but we are planning on
inviting her to baptism in one of our next lessons=E2=80=A6 =F0=9F=A4=94=F0=
=9F=91=80

Saturday
=E2=80=A6so! First off today Apparently Sakurako met with the Abeno Mission=
aries
(my two past comps, Sonomura=E9=95=B7=E8=80=81 and Martinson=E9=95=B7=E8=80=
=81=F0=9F=98=86) and they invited her to
baptism, and she said yes =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=B2 She's our friend so we w=
ill probably be the
ones to Baptize her but it was a funny turn of events. We were able to call
with her and talk about things. The most difficult part for her is going to
be telling her Mom about it. She's really worried about it, so we are going
to try and have lessons with members who had similar experiences. Today we
had Eikaiwa at Ozaki, and on our way back home we went to the church and
finished up some pizza members made for an activity. Later we had an
Apartment inspection over video chat and it was Hilarious. Brother Watanabe
is such an awesome guy, but he definitely surprised us with some of his
comments. He said that getting bald stinks, but he could probably just find
a truck on the street and he wouldn't have to worry about his hair loss
anymore =F0=9F=92=80 pretty crazy comment. After the inspection, we went to=
 leave and
try to do some housing. On the way, we literally watched an old lady crash
her car into the back of a building. She broke her back window and the back
of her car, but the store was ok I think. It's lucky nobody was in the way.
Our actual housing today was pretty lackluster, a lot of people saying no.
We had a few nice refusals, however, and one person might have interest in
our Eikaiwa class!

Sunday
Pretty normal Sunday Today, I Gave the closing prayer in Sacrament meeting
which was nice, definitely not my best prayer but its the effort that
counts. Later we visited Sister Aren with Sister Suehiro, and dropped Off
some treats. They seem to be having a pretty tough time, mostly just the
mom, Sister Aren. We read a scripture together, and invited her to read the
whole chapter. She has a very strong testimony! Keep her in your prayers!

Imma Write about Pday next week, but it's in general been a pretty solid
week. I feel that this email is missing some sauce, so it's poetry time
baby.

Haiku

Piping hot, Cheesy
It's not a corny romance
It is Pizza Hut.

Mind in the Gutter?

To what extent can you tune out the static?
That white noise that surrounds
What do you hear that gets the =E2=80=9Call clear=E2=80=9D
Have you thoroughly examined your intake?

How well-dusted is your attic?
What, in your mind, abounds?
If revealed, would you have cause to fear?
I recommend you check, and make no mistake.

I hope you enjoyed my poetry lol. I am gonna try and keep things pretty
short for today, but I want everyone reading this to know that they are
awesome! I love getting the chance to serve a mission, and I've learned so
many good things about myself and what I want my life to be like once I'm
back in America. I miss you all, and I'm almost a year into my mission! I
will be looking forward to sharing my experiences with you all in person =
=F0=9F=98=81

Love you guys!

--00000000000039fcbb0638c48d00
